  "implemented_behavior": "Finite forward Horn-rule proof checking with trusted facts and no invented premises.",
  "bounded_contract": "Reference: facts {id,atom}, rules {id,antecedents,consequent}, weighted goals {id,atom,weight}. Candidate steps: id,rule_id,premises,conclusion.\nOnly trusted facts or valid preceding steps can support premises. Premise atoms must equal the complete antecedent set. Invalid/forward/circular steps do not enter the proven set; step IDs cannot shadow fact IDs. Rule conclusion must match exactly.\nGoals earn all-or-zero weight when available from trusted/valid proof. Any invalid extra step yields FAIL even if all requested goals earn credit. Score and outcome must be consumed together.",
  "bounds_and_open_scope": "This is a bounded formal proof calculus, not validation of arbitrary natural-language reasoning, induction, analogy, uncertainty, temporal or spatial reasoning. Such adapters require additional governed work.",
